    "prompt": "This is an original practice task. You should spend about 20 minutes on this task. The table below shows results from a visitor-flow evaluation at Harbridge Museum during three weekends in March 2025. The data combine sensor counts with 412 exit questionnaires. The South Gallery was closed for maintenance during the second weekend, so its figures are based on two weekends only. Gallery | Average visitors per hour | Average dwell time in minutes | Visitors rating crowding as high | Visitors rating experience as good or excellent: Entrance Hall | 210 | 8 | 18% | 82% | North Wing - Local History | 95 | 22 | 12% | 88% | East Wing - Natural World | 165 | 19 | 47% | 64% | South Gallery - Temporary Exhibition | 140 | 26 | 52% | 71% | Riverside Cafe and Shop | 120 | 15 | 21% | 90%. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Note any important qualifications or limits in the data. Write at least 150 words.",
