    "task": "Task 2 · River Access and Environmental Care",
    "pathwayStage": "band-6-5",
    "focus": "Balancing recreation, safety and protection of riversides",
    "prompt": "This is an original practice task. You should spend about 40 minutes on this task. Many local councils want to improve public access to rivers like the River Cole by building paths, steps, parking and signs. Some residents welcome easier access for walking, paddling and fishing. Others worry that more visitors will cause litter, disturbance to wildlife and safety problems if maintenance budgets are limited. To what extent do you agree that councils should expand river access even when long-term maintenance cannot be fully guaranteed? Give reasons for your answer and include relevant examples. Acknowledge limitations and situations where your argument may not apply. Write at least 250 words.",
    "minimumWords": 250,
    "suggestedMinutes": 40
