    "exam": "IELTS Academic · Task 2",
    "skill": "Writing",
    "task": "Task 2 · Community Heritage Interview Project",
    "pathwayStage": "band-6",
    "focus": "paraphrase, linked ideas and evaluation of accuracy",
    "prompt": "A community heritage project asks young people to interview older people in their community about their lives and local history. Some people think this is a valuable way to learn about the past. Others think information from interviews is not always accurate or useful. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. Give reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience. Write at least 250 words in about 40 minutes.",
