    "skill": "Writing",
    "task": "Task 2 · Representing Missing Observations in Public Reports",
    "pathwayStage": "band-7",
    "focus": "honest communication of incomplete evidence and trade-offs in visualisation",
    "prompt": "When data is missing for a period (for example, because a survey was cancelled or a sensor failed), some reports leave a gap or mark the data as unavailable, while others estimate the missing value to keep the trend line complete.\n\nDiscuss the advantages and disadvantages of each approach. What principles should guide how missing observations are shown to the public? Give reasons for your answer and support them with examples, considering clarity, honesty, and the risk of misleading the audience.",
